"""Data-linked manuscript additions for the prescribing-gap and spend audits."""


def render(read):
    gap = read('paper/prescription_gap_audit.json')['mean_counts_and_metrics']['rxrsi_selected']
    read('upgrade_v21/results/development_capacity_audit.json')
    spend = read('paper/total_spend_audit.json')
    low, high = spend['located_successful_reported_usd_range']
    gap_text = r'''\paragraph{Where historical order agreement is lost.}
A post hoc recount of the frozen historical pipeline separates vocabulary, selection and order-field failures. ''' + f"The pipeline predicts {gap['pred']/gap['cases']:.2f} drugs per admission against {gap['gold']/gap['cases']:.2f} recorded targets, while omitting {gap['false_negative']/gap['cases']:.2f} targets and adding {gap['false_positive']/gap['cases']:.2f} reference-relative extras. {100*(1-gap['oov_fraction_of_false_negatives']):.2f}\\% of missed targets are inside the fixed vocabulary. Recall is {100*gap['prior_target_recall']:.2f}\\% for targets already present in prior available orders, versus {100*gap['new_target_recall']:.2f}\\% for other targets. Among complete reference Core4 tuples whose drug is predicted, {100*gap['core4_recall_conditional_on_correct_drug']:.2f}\\% match all four fields. " + r'''These are mean counts/metrics across three seeds, not current LLM-agent results. In-vocabulary misses locate a selection gap without establishing its clinical cause. Extra orders are not automatically inappropriate. Separate proposal-only support diagnostics cover80.80\% of target drugs; perfect reference-informed selection would reach89.25\% drug F1, an oracle ceiling rather than achieved performance. This post hoc test analysis neither selects a repair nor supplies learning feedback.

\paragraph{Mechanism hypotheses and human alignment.}
Recorded prescriptions expose clinician actions, not their complete reasoning or a uniquely appropriate regimen. Agreement should therefore be supplemented by treatment-goal coverage, acceptable alternatives, joint order correctness and clinician edit burden. The case evidence suggests testable workflow hypotheses: product retrieval can lose a necessary condition; genuine quotations can coexist with unsupported patient premises; and treatment-phase errors can survive label retrieval. Establishing a mechanism requires changing one stage while holding cases and resources fixed, observing the intermediate decision change, and confirming corrections without regressions on independent cases. Patient-condition overgeneralization and harmful memory are already studied by MedPIC, GRASP and SkeMex \citep{medpic,grasp,skemex}; we do not claim those broad phenomena as new discoveries. No neural-circuit mechanism is established here.
'''
    cost_text = r'''\paragraph{Cumulative response expenditure.}
''' + f"The located successful-response costs across the upgrade studies total approximately USD{(low+high)/2:.2f}: USD{spend['main_ledger']['reported_usd']:.5f} in {spend['main_ledger']['successful_response_events']:,} shared-ledger events, plus USD{spend['legacy']['deduplicated_recorded_usd']:.5f}--{spend['legacy']['all_records_usd']:.5f} in legacy records. " + r'''The narrow range reflects ambiguous identical pilot/full-run records, not bounds on unrecorded charges. Cached rereads are not added; separately logged repeated requests are retained. Six legacy records lack prices, and failed requests, local compute, earlier unrecorded work and account adjustments remain unreconciled. This is provider-reported receipt cost, not an invoice. Previously reported study increments are already included. The audit itself performs no model calls.
'''
    return gap_text, cost_text
